## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical CISSP concepts for edge-to-cloud security in a high-velocity fleet context, including hardware-backed identity, secure update, provenance, and incident response.

## Key Concepts

- Edge attestation with TPM/TEE
- Ephemeral credentials and mTLS
- SBOM and reproducible builds (Sigstore/SLSA)
- Runtime integrity and OTA security
- Incident response, tabletop exercises, and tooling

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: verify firmware signature on boot
function verifyFirmware(signature, payload) {
  const isValid = verifySignature(payload, signature);
  if (!isValid) throw new Error('Invalid firmware');
  bootMeetsIntegrityChecks();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale attestation verification across 200k devices?
- What tooling would you use for SBOM generation and artifact signing at the edge?

This question tests CISSP-aligned incident response and forensics skills in a serverless, multi-cloud context. It evaluates understanding of detection telemetry, containment procedures, evidence handling, chain of custody maintenance, and cross-provider playbooks.

Key Concepts

- Incident response lifecycles across AWS Lambda, Google Cloud Functions, and on-premises FaaS
- Evidence preservation and time synchronization across cloud providers
- Cross-cloud playbooks and tooling coordination

Code Example

```javascript
// Example: mock evidence hash calculation
const crypto = require('crypto');

function calculateEvidenceHash(filePath, content) {
  const hash = crypto.createHash('sha256');
  hash.update(content);
  const evidenceHash = hash.digest('hex');

  return {
    filePath,
    evidenceHash,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
  };
}

module.exports = { calculateEvidenceHash };
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical zero-trust for admin access, mirroring real enterprise risk of credential theft and lateral movement in hybrid environments.

## Key Concepts
- Zero-trust, device posture, MFA, PIM, Just-In-Time
- Jump hosts, session recording, RBAC, break-glass, SIEM/audit

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-policy: grant only if posture true and MFA passed
if (device.posture && user.mfa && time.inWindow) {
  grantAccess();
} else {
  denyAccess();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure effectiveness (MTTR, number of break-glass events)?
- How would this adapt to cloud-native IAM vs PAM solutions across AWS/Azure?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design edge-scale supply chain controls and incident response across thousands of devices, including hardware attestation, ephemeral credentials, and cross-region governance.

## Key Concepts

- Edge attestation (TPM/IMA)
- Ephemeral credentials (SPIFFE/SPIRE)
- Reproducible builds and SBOM
- Artifact signing and verification
- Canary deployments and rollback
- Cross-region auditing and incident response

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal artifact verification sketch
function verifyArtifact(artifact, signature, sbom) {
  // Verify signature against trusted keys
  if (!verifySignature(signature, artifact)) {
    throw new Error('Invalid signature');
  }

  // Validate SBOM integrity
  if (!validateSBOM(sbom)) {
    throw new Error('Invalid SBOM');
  }

  // Check reproducible build hash
  return verifyReproducibleHash(artifact, sbom);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical IAM/ABAC decisions across multi-cloud data platforms, focusing on least privilege, policy enforcement, and incident readiness.

## Key Concepts
- Identity federation, SCIM provisioning, OIDC/SAML
- ABAC vs RBAC, policy-as-code (OPA)
- Ephemeral secrets (Vault), data masking, auditability
- IR tabletop design, validation steps, tooling choices

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple ABAC evaluation: user can access dataset if in allowed teams and has data-privilege role
function canAccess(user, resource, action){
  if(!user.roles.includes('data-privilege')) return false;
  if(!resource.allowedTeams.includes(user.team)) return false;
  if(action==='write' && !user.roles.includes('data-writer')) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you detect privilege creep and revoke expired permissions?
- Which logging/monitoring signals are key for a cross-cloud IR tabletop?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests threat modeling and practical controls for log integrity across cloud boundaries, a common fintech risk.

## Key Concepts
- Log integrity, STRIDE/PASTA, SBOM, log signing, KMS, append-only storage, WORM, cross-cloud replication, SIEM/SOAR, tabletop exercises

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo code for signing log entries
function signLogEntry(entry, key) {
  const signature = crypto.sign("SHA256", Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(entry)), key);
  return { entry, signature };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify integrity of logs during audits across clouds?
- How would you coordinate key rotation and revocation in a distributed SIEM?
